### Phase 9: transfers. payment-service calls account-service over REST (token relay).
### NOTE: since Phase 10 the request takes "targetAccountNumber" (10 digits) instead of
### "targetAccountId". This file documents Phase 9 as it was; use phase-10.http against current code.
### Tokens:  ./infrastructure/keycloak/pkce-login.sh <alice|bob|sam> 2>/dev/null

@gw = http://localhost:8080
@alice = paste-alice-token
@bob = paste-bob-token
@sam = paste-sam-token
@savings = paste-alice-thb-account-id-1
@checking = paste-alice-thb-account-id-2
@usd = paste-alice-usd-account-id
@bobsAccount = paste-a-bob-account-id
@paymentId = paste-a-payment-id

### ---------- setup: Alice's accounts (Phase 8 endpoints) ----------

### Open a THB account (run twice for savings + checking; once with "USD")
POST {{gw}}/api/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "SAVINGS", "currency": "THB" }

### Fund the savings account
POST {{gw}}/api/accounts/{{savings}}/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 500.00 }

### ---------- transfers ----------

### 201 COMPLETED: between Alice's own accounts
POST {{gw}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{savings}}", "targetAccountId": "{{checking}}", "amount": 120.00, "description": "rent" }

### 422 INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS (account-service's code, passed through)
POST {{gw}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{savings}}", "targetAccountId": "{{checking}}", "amount": 9999.00 }

### 422 CURRENCY_MISMATCH
POST {{gw}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{savings}}", "targetAccountId": "{{usd}}", "amount": 1.00 }

### 422 TARGET_ACCOUNT_NOT_FOUND: Alice → Bob. Token relay can't do this (fixed in Phase 10)
POST {{gw}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{savings}}", "targetAccountId": "{{bobsAccount}}", "amount": 10.00 }

### 422 SOURCE_ACCOUNT_NOT_FOUND: Bob tries to pay from Alice's account (account-service ownership check)
POST {{gw}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{savings}}", "targetAccountId": "{{bobsAccount}}", "amount": 50.00 }

### 400: same source and target, too many decimals
POST {{gw}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{savings}}", "targetAccountId": "{{savings}}", "amount": 1.005 }

### Stop account-service now, then send this → 503 + Retry-After, status FAILED, nothing moved
POST {{gw}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{savings}}", "targetAccountId": "{{checking}}", "amount": 5.00 }

### ---------- history ----------

### Alice's payments, newest first (rejected and failed ones included)
GET {{gw}}/api/payments?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### One payment
GET {{gw}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### Bob asks for Alice's payment → 404
GET {{gw}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}

### ---------- back office ----------

### SUPPORT: reconciliation work queue
GET {{gw}}/api/admin/payments?status=NEEDS_RECONCILIATION
Authorization: Bearer {{sam}}

### SUPPORT: everything, newest first
GET {{gw}}/api/admin/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{sam}}

### SUPPORT can't send money → 403
POST {{gw}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{sam}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sourceAccountId": "{{savings}}", "targetAccountId": "{{checking}}", "amount": 1.00 }
